WOW-BG3 benilla patch 0056: what WoW has under BG3's pointer, in the log.

- wowbg3_lead.rs, `forward_pointer`: every time the hover record changes, one line says whether a
  click where BG3's pointer is would be WoW's (a corpse to loot, an object, an NPC WoW claims), BG3's
  (a mirrored mob, whose stand-in takes the click) or neither, with the unit, corpse and object guids,
  WoW's cursor kind and the quest-giver status. On change only, so it costs nothing in a quiet frame.
- Why: looting and talking to quest givers stopped working in 0.1.0, and the two halves of that path
  (WoW's pick and the click routing) cannot be told apart from the logs there are. A desktop session
  with this line answers it: a line that never names a unit while the pointer sits on one puts the
  fault in the pick, one that names it while a click does nothing puts it in the routing. Release mode
  cannot test it at all, as it is headless and BG3 reports a fixed pointer there.

--- a/crates/benilla-app/src/wowbg3_lead.rs
+++ b/crates/benilla-app/src/wowbg3_lead.rs
@@ -669,6 +669,21 @@
     if key != link.hover_flags || link.hover_seq == 0 {
         link.hover_flags = key;
         link.hover_seq = link.hover_seq.wrapping_add(1).max(1);
+        // What WoW has under BG3's pointer, each time it changes: whether a click there is WoW's
+        // (flag 2: a corpse to loot, an object, an NPC WoW claims), BG3's (flag 4: a mirrored mob,
+        // whose stand-in takes the click) or neither. A line that never names a unit while the
+        // pointer sits on one says the pick is at fault; one that names it while nothing happens on
+        // a click says the routing is.
+        info!(
+            "wowbg3 hover: flags {flags} (WoW's UI {}, WoW's to click {}, a mirrored mob {}), \
+             unit {:?}, corpse {:?}, object {:?}, cursor {kind}, quest status {status}",
+            over_ui.0,
+            flags & 2 != 0,
+            flags & 4 != 0,
+            hovered.guid,
+            hovered.corpse_guid,
+            object.guid,
+        );
         // 36 bytes since patch 0047: the 28 of 0019, the status at 28 and the seq again at 32.
         let mut rec = [0u8; 36];
         rec[0..4].copy_from_slice(b"WBH1");
